  {
   "a": "CVS",
   "b": "RCVS",
   "what": "Diuretics, RAAS, hypertension, heart failure, angina and lipids appear in both. Merge them into one branch; antiarrhythmics exist only in Renal & CVS."
  }
 ],
 "cards": {
  "digoxin": {
   "title": "Digoxin",
   "path": [
    "Pharmacology",
    "Renal & Cardiovascular",
    "Heart failure"
   ],
   "en": "Digoxin makes a failing heart pump harder and beat slower. It blocks the Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase pump in heart cells. Sodium builds up inside, so the cell pushes out less calcium. More calcium inside means a stronger contraction. It also acts on the vagus nerve, which slows the heart rate. It is used for heart failure and atrial fibrillation. The main danger is its narrow therapeutic index: the helpful dose and the toxic dose are close. Low potassium makes toxicity much more likely, which is why digoxin given with most diuretics needs close watching.",
   "am": "ዲጎክሲን (Digoxin) የደከመ ልብ በኃይል እንዲመታ እና ምቱ እንዲቀንስ ያደርጋል። በልብ ሴሎች ውስጥ ያለውን Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase pump ያግዳል። በዚህ ምክንያት Na⁺ በሴሉ ውስጥ ይከማቻል፣ ሴሉም Ca²⁺ን ወደ ውጭ የሚያስወጣው ይቀንሳል። በሴሉ ውስጥ ብዙ Ca²⁺ ሲኖር መኮማተሩ (contraction) ይጠነክራል። በተጨማሪም vagus nerve ላይ ስለሚሰራ የልብ ምት (heart rate) ይቀንሳል። ለ heart failure እና ለ atrial fibrillation ይሰጣል። ዋናው አደጋ narrow therapeutic index ነው፤ የሚያክመው መጠን እና የሚመርዘው መጠን በጣም ይቀራረባሉ። K⁺ ዝቅተኛ ሲሆን (hypokalemia) toxicity በቀላሉ ይከሰታል፤ ስለዚህ ከ diuretics ጋር ሲሰጥ በጥንቃቄ መከታተል ያስፈልጋል።",
